course: dictionary
lesson: 13355
title: Handset: the phone you hold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A handset is a thing you hold in your hand. The word is built from two parts: hand and set. «Lily picked up the handset and dialled Grandma's number.» Here the handset is the part of the phone you hold to your ear and mouth.
explain: Clues in the sentence show you the meaning. «The shop had a sale on mobile handsets.» Mobile tells you the phone can be carried around, so a handset here is a mobile phone. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A phone fits, so handset must mean phone.
explain: «The cordless handset was on the sofa, so Dad could walk round the house while he talked.» Cordless means it has no wire joining it to the wall. Handsets can also be hand-held remote controls or other devices, so check the clues each time.
fact: Handset means the part of a telephone that you hold to your ear and mouth.
fact: Handset can also mean a mobile phone, and shops often use the word this way.
fact: Handset can mean a hand-held remote control or device.
fact: A mobile handset is a phone you can carry about with you.
fact: A cordless handset has no wire, so you can move around while you talk.
exercise: «Lily picked up the handset and dialled Grandma's number.» What is the handset? | A plate for food | A kind of shoe | * The part of a phone you hold to your ear and mouth
exercise: «The shop had a sale on mobile handsets.» What does handset mean in this sentence? | * A mobile phone | A house with a garden | A type of bread
exercise: In «a cordless handset», which word tells you it has no wire? | * cordless | a | handset
test: Ben said, «Pass me the remote handset, please.» What does handset mean here? | A kind of hat | * A hand-held remote control or device | A pencil case
test: «She held the handset to her ear and waited for the call.» What does handset mean in this sentence? | * The part of a phone you hold | A bedroom | A dinner plate
exam: Which phrase uses handset to mean a phone you can carry around? | * mobile handset | a hand-made card | a bowl of soup | a set of tools
